  "tone": {
   "ok": false,
   "issues": [
    "The headline's trailing clause 'after global outage' names the setback event directly even though the main clause already supplies the upside (apologises, restores services); every accepted headline example in the brief drops the setback noun entirely instead of naming it even briefly (e.g. 'Railways bring abuse into the open as industry steps up protection for staff', 'Unions and ministers work on rescue deal to keep steelworks open'), so 'outage' should move out of the headline into the standfirst, which already states it."
